[stage3] LEARNING (timeout-race pattern): Promise.race([fetch, sleep(N)]) is a TWO-bug trap on a Worker hot path — (1) the losing sleep leaks an armed timer per call (delays isolate teardown), (2) fetch is never aborted so the in-flight request outlives the client's give-up (double-submission window on money paths). Correct pattern: AbortController + setTimeout(()=>controller.abort()), pass signal to fetch, clearTimeout in finally. Fresh controller PER attempt (not shared across retries). Keep injected sleep/random for BACKOFF only so fake-timer jitter tests stay deterministic. Apply to T15 viemSigner (receipt wait / submit) and T20 (receipt-wait timeout vs revert).
